The source itself is confused about this, on further investigation.

Nothing in zap.c calls golemeffects(), (unlike ugolemeffects()); this
means that your wand of fire and spell of fireball won't do anything
particularly special to an iron golem, which is MR_FIRE.

Some things in uhitm.c do call golemeffects(), but it looks as though you
have to actually be polymorphed into something that does fire damage,
such as a salamander (in which case both straw and paper golems will be
instakilled, and iron golems will be healed by your attacks).

Wielding Fire Brand and swatting an iron golem, on the other hand, 
doesn't cut it; but then, there are no calls to golemeffects() in that 
chain of code.

Reading a scroll of fire will create an explosion centered on yourself,
and this _does_ call golemeffects().

It looks like a big swathe of inconsistency, in short.

